urces></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-61242118-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>61242118</doc-number><kind>A</kind> </document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-63179624-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>63179624</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-7072822-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>7072822</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4325055-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4325055</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5696509-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5696509</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1047039A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>OZAWA TOKURO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>SEIKO EPSON CORP</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>OZAWA, TOKURO</last-name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>OZAWA TOKURO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>OZAWA, TOKURO</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>In step 1, a switch is off, and a first charger (C1) charges parasitic capacitance (CS). In step 2, the switch (SW) is kept off and a second charger (C2) charges internal capacitance (CD). In step 3, the switch (SW) is turned on.  Then, the charge in the internal capacitance (CD) flows into the parasitic capacitance (CS), and the voltage across the internal capacitance (CD) finally becomes equal to the voltage across the parasitic capacitance (CS). In step 4, the switch (SW) is turned off again, and the second charger (C2) charges the internal capacitance (CD). The voltage across the parasitic capacitance (CS) can be adjusted to a desired value by repeating steps 3 and 4.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Aux fins de l'invention, on distingue une étape 1 dans laquelle un commutateur est à l'état bloqué, avec un premier chargeur (C1) chargeant une capacité parasite (CS); une étape 2 dans laquelle le commutateur (SW) est maintenu à l'état bloqué, avec un second chargeur (C2) chargeant une capacité interne (CD); une étape 3 dans laquelle le commutateur (SW) est à l'état passant, moyennant quoi la charge de la capacité interne (CD) passe dans la capacité parasite (CS) et la tension aux bornes de la capacité interne (CD) devient finalement égale à la tension aux bornes de la capacité parasite (CS); une étape 4 dans laquelle le commutateur (SW) est de nouveau à l'état bloqué, avec le second chargeur (C2) chargeant la capacité interne (CD). La tension aux bornes de la capacité parasite (CS) peut être réglée à tel ou tel niveau souhaité, par répétition des étapes 3 et 4.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>